        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I feel `cmd.exe` in this case is an exception, It's the only program we've encountered that requires `\\` path separator to launch. 😅\n\n>  It doesn't work with my own config, which sets pwsh and all the shell* options, so I guess I need to fix that.\n\nBTW, in PR #40031, we've tried to provide reasonable default values for `shell*` options for most shells.",
            "created_at": "2026-07-19T14:32:07Z",
